  "prompt": "Use case: stylized-concept\nAsset type: ONE new transparent production spritesheet containing EXACTLY EIGHT independent mobile board-game UI illustrations. Wide landscape, target 2048 x 1024 pixels, four columns by two rows. Each equal cell contains one object only. Real alpha background, generous fully transparent gutters, no contact or overlap across cells.\nPrimary request: newly draw a coherent set of friendly toy-like 2D game reward and mission icons with a polished miniature 3D-diorama impression. Match the warm cream, mint/sea-green, gold and rich accent palette, chunky readable proportions and restrained internal form shading of a cute coastal construction board-game. These are original new artwork, never pasted screenshot pixels.\nExact layout, left to right:\nTOP ROW, cell 1: a mint-green diamond-shaped board tile, a square rotated 45 degrees with a darker green edge and a slight bevel. Its center is COMPLETELY BLANK so native UI text can be placed there later. NO GO letters, no marks, no arrows, no symbols in this tile.\nTOP ROW, cell 2: a small friendly mischievous toy bank-robber face icon wearing a black top hat with a dark navy band, round little nose, curled white moustache and a playful expression. Head and hat only, compact silhouette, original generic cartoon character rather than a branded mascot, no body, no weapon, no money bag.\nTOP ROW, cell 3: a small upright smartphone with a pale cream body, dark edge, mint screen and one large green upgrade arrow curling upward on the screen. A tiny speaker may be geometric but there must be no letters, numerals, status text, dots that resemble written text, app labels or checkmarks.\nTOP ROW, cell 4: one SMALL GREEN REWARD CARD PACK, a bright green sealed foil packet with crimped top/bottom and a simple lighter green inset panel. Blank unbranded pack, a slight friendly tilt.\nBOTTOM ROW, cell 1: one SMALL ORANGE-BROWN REWARD CARD PACK, terracotta/orange foil with warm brown edges, crimped ends and a simple lighter inset panel, same family and proportions as the green pack.\nBOTTOM ROW, cell 2: one SMALL YELLOW REWARD CARD PACK, sunny yellow-gold foil with orange edges and a simple lighter inset panel, same family as the other small packs.\nBOTTOM ROW, cell 3: ONE pale gray toy die in three-quarter perspective with rounded cube edges and clear black circular pips on its visible faces. Pips are allowed, but no numerals or text. No stack, no second die.\nBOTTOM ROW, cell 4: ONE LARGE PURPLE REWARD CARD PACK, rich violet/magenta foil with bright purple edges and crimped ends, slightly taller and wider in visual weight than the small packs. Simple lighter inset panel, blank and unbranded.\nComposition: all eight complete objects fully visible with no clipping, each centered in its own cell, exactly eight separated silhouettes. Consistent soft light, warm clean toy materials, broad readable forms, just enough depth for a mobile-game icon. Keep the packaging surfaces simple and readable at small sizes.\nText: NONE anywhere. No letters, words, GO, numbers, price, currency, badges, logos, emblems, symbols that look like a brand seal, watermark or labels. The die may have circular pips and the phone may have the specified green arrow.\nTransparency: preserve true empty alpha outside every object. No opaque background, no checkerboard picture, no white canvas, no tile/card frame, no circle backing behind icons, no scenery, no shared ground, no UI panel. NO external drop/cast/contact shadows or glow outside each object's own silhouette; the engine will add UI shadow. Internal object shading is allowed. No extra floating decorations or tiny debris.",
